`@builder/web/page` reads browser state each time you call a getter. Import it
explicitly in a `.moth` file.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    @builder/web/page

    address = page.url()
    listed = page.sync_navigation("nav") catch then false
    io.line([: [address] [listed]])
]

`sync_navigation` is optional. It needs a navigation root with the hooks
described in @#page (@builder/web/page advanced). Call it again after History API
changes.

`page.url()` reads the live browser address at runtime. In contrast,
@../site (@builder/web/site)'s `site.url` builds static links at compile time.
